content.text:
The auth tests do test the app. Mutation score on the auth code is **69.7%** (101 of 145 mutants killed), up from 56.6% on the first run. I added 11 tests to close the real gaps, so the auth suite is now 31 tests, all green. The suite runs in about 0.8s and lint is clean. Nothing from this step is committed.

**Setup finding**
Stryker's vitest runner (`@stryker-mutator/vitest-runner` 10.0.0) does not work with the repo's vitest 5.0.3. Every mutant reported as surviving with zero tests run, even though my manual 7-vs-8 character check showed the tests do catch that change. I switched to Stryker's generic command runner, which runs `npx vitest run` once per mutant. That takes about a minute for 145 mutants.

- **Scope:** `apps/user-ui/stryker.config.json` mutates only the auth code in `App.tsx` (session check, sign-in and sign-out handlers, the password handler, and the sign-in and password-change screens). These are four line ranges.
- **Install location:** Stryker is installed in `/tmp/claude-501/stryker-tools`, not in the repo, so no lockfile churn. It needs a local port, so I ran it with the sandbox off, which asked you for permission. This setup is not repeatable on another machine yet.
- **To rerun:** `node /tmp/claude-501/stryker-tools/node_modules/.bin/stryker run stryker.config.json` from `apps/user-ui`.
- **Housekeeping:** I added `apps/user-ui/.stryker-tmp/` and `apps/user-ui/reports/` to `.gitignore`.

**The 44 mutants still alive**
- **19 are workspace resets in sign-out** (channels, agents, events, drafts, unread counts, deep link). They only show up with workspace data, so the sidebar, timeline and dialogs suites should kill them.
- **About 22 are dead or equivalent code, left alone:**
  - the short-password and mismatch messages in the handler (the button is disabled before they can run);
  - the "Signing in..." label (hidden by the loading screen);
  - the "Unable to ..." fallbacks;
  - `preventDefault`;
  - redundant `setError(null)` calls;
  - empty-username fallbacks.
- **About 3 are minor:**
  - the fields cleared after a successful update while still on the screen;
  - the user id read from the session;
  - the `username || loginUsername` fallback in the password update request (unreachable).

**The 11 new tests**
- the "Loading OrgOps..." screen while the session is checked;
- a session with no username counts as signed out;
- the sign-in form is prefilled with the last operator's name and an empty password after sign-out;
- a failed session check after a password update returns to the sign-in form;
- a half-typed new password is cleared on sign-out;
- the username shows on the password-change screen;
- surrounding spaces are ignored when counting length and when comparing with the confirmation;
- the password is sent without surrounding spaces;
- the button shows "Updating..." and is disabled while the update is pending;
- the operator can retry after a rejected update.

The first mutation run also showed my initial suite was weak on trimming, loading states and sign-out side effects, which these tests now cover.

I haven't ticked 0c or 0b in the todo, since only auth is done. Next is the workspace-load suite, unless you'd rather commit this first.
